    77	### 1.1 Arm H — pad-and-batch: the exact tensor program (`fullmodel/padbatch.py`)
    78	Notation: bands i = 0..59, widths K_i (`dim_inputs`), S = ΣK_i, o_i = Σ_{h<i}K_h,
    79	K_max = max K_i, T frames, D = 384, hidden 1536.
    80	- `band_split` input `(1, T, S)` → append one zero column → `(T, S+1)`;
    81	  gather with `I[i,j] = o_i + j` for `j < K_i`, else `S` (the zero column) →
    82	  `(T, 60, K_max)` → **transpose to band-major `(60, T, K_max)`**;
    83	  `F.normalize(dim=-1)` (fp32, torch's default eps) × per-band scale
    84	  `(60,1,1) = K_i**0.5` × zero-padded gamma `(60, 1, K_max)`; then
    85	  `baddbmm(b_pad (60,1,D), x_norm (60,T,K_max), W_pad (60,K_max,D))` with
    86	  `W_pad[i, :K_i, :] = W_iᵀ` and zero rows beyond K_i, `b_pad[i] = b_i`;
    87	  transpose back to `(1, T, 60, D)` = the stock `torch.stack(dim=-2)` order.
    88	  Algebra: zero entries add nothing to the L2 norm, so the padded normalize
    89	  equals the per-band normalize; zero weight rows contribute 0.
    90	- `mask_estimators[·]` input `(1, T, 60, D)` → band-major `(60, T, D)`;
    91	  hidden layers j: `tanh(baddbmm(b_j (60,1,H), h, W_j (60,·,H)))` with every
    92	  original bias kept; last layer: `baddbmm(b_last, h, W_last (60, 1536, 2K_max))`
    93	  where, for the original last weight `W_iᵀ (1536, 2K_i)` and bias `b_i`,
    94	  original columns `j < K_i` go to column `j` and original columns `K_i + j`
    95	  go to column `K_max + j` (same mapping for the bias; other columns zero);
    96	  `F.glu(dim=-1)` on width `2K_max` then equals the per-band GLU for `j < K_i`
    97	  and yields `0·σ(0) = 0` in pad columns; time-major flatten `(T, 60·K_max)`
    98	  and gather `J = concat_i(i·K_max + arange(K_i))` → `(1, T, S)` = the stock
    99	  `torch.cat(dim=-1)` band-concatenation order (duplicated frequencies
   100	  included; the forward's later overlap scatter/averaging is untouched).
   101	- Autocast: `baddbmm` autocasts all three operands to fp16 exactly as
   102	  `nn.Linear` autocasts `F.linear`, so hidden/output dtypes match the stock
   103	  path (fp16 after every affine; fp32 normalize). Padded weights/biases are
   104	  derived buffers built once from the original parameters (no parameter is
   105	  modified). Claim: **algebraic equivalence**, verified numerically at the
   106	  loose tier (H is compiled; reduction trees and fusion differ) — never
   107	  bitwise. A validation failure makes H INVALID and is reported, not tuned.
