   189	## 4. Boundary-cost microbenchmark (plan 0.4; design registered, owner reviews)
   190	`fullmodel/boundary_bench.py`: chains of N **dependent** kernels, N ∈ {10,
   191	100, 1000, 2000}: (trivial) one Triton program loads ONE int32 element, adds
   192	1, stores it back to the same buffer — kernel k+1 depends on kernel k, and
   193	the final counter must equal the total launch count (exact-integer
   194	dependency proof); (elem37) an in-place value-preserving fp16 elementwise op
   195	on a 37 MB tensor, N ∈ {10, 100}; (gemm) alternating dependent GEMMs
   196	660×384×1536 / 660×1536×384 fp16 into preallocated ping-pong outputs with
   197	1/√K-scaled weights (bounded values), N ∈ {10, 100}. Modes: stream launches;
   198	one CUDA graph of the chain (replayed); programmatic dependent launch for the
   199	trivial chain (Triton 3.4 `launch_pdl=True`; `gdc_wait()` before the
   200	dependent load, `gdc_launch_dependents()` after the store; the PTX is checked
   201	for `griddepcontrol`), on a stream and inside a graph; real-kernel PDL is
   202	UNSUPPORTED through cuBLAS/ATen launches and recorded as such. Timing:
   203	unprofiled device time via CUDA events around the chain, median of 20
   204	repeats with min/max → `T(N)` per (chain, mode), plus least-squares slope
   205	and intercept over N. **`T(N)/N` and the slope are effective per-node service
   206	times INCLUDING kernel execution — not boundary costs.** A separate
   207	node-level trace of the same script yields, per chain segment (NVTX), the
   208	median kernel duration and the median serial inter-kernel gap; for non-PDL
   209	modes the serial gap is the boundary estimate; for PDL modes kernels overlap
   210	and no subtraction is attempted (pure boundary `UNRESOLVED`); the traced
   211	run's perturbation vs the unprofiled `T(N)` is reported. Prior calibration
   212	points to compare against: Hazy (H100 ≈ 2.1 µs stream, ≈ 1.3 µs graph);
   213	NVIDIA's CUDA 12.6 figure ≈ 0.55 µs/node is empty-kernel graph device
   214	service time (RTX 3060), not CPU launch cost. **Until measured, no
   215	per-boundary number is used anywhere**, and the ledger's X10 must not count
   216	kernel execution as removable boundary overhead. Any unavailable mode is
   217	recorded `UNTESTED(reason)`.
